WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:07.420
Enter monthly sales, compare tenants, and bill the share of sales above the breakpoint.

2
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:13.930
Turnover and sales follows what each tenant sells, and the rent they owe on it.

3
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:19.370
Total sales, sales per square metre, and the rent to sales ratio.

4
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:24.610
Each month, enter the sales on the Sales tab.

5
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:29.610
Type the gross sales, the returns and the number of receipts.

6
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:41.440
Choose Save sales. Tenants can also send them from their portal.

7
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.790
Then open Billing.

8
00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:53.370
Turnover rent is the sales above the breakpoint, times the agreed percentage. When sales are below it, nothing is owed.

9
00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:59.160
Bill each lease, or record nil, so the month is closed.

10
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:05.160
Billed months move down. On the overview, the ranking compares every tenant's sales.
